  "evidence": "TEXT_C: Maintain the Human Rights Act and ECHR; oppose blanket data retention with targeted, overseen extremism measures; appoint an LGBTI rights envoy; extend votes to 16–17. Strongly pro‑EU (continued membership with a double‑majority to leave; greater devolved roles in EU decision‑making). Green/anti‑nuclear defence stance (fracking moratorium; ambitious carbon targets and renewables; oppose renewal of the UK nuclear deterrent). Reintroduce a post‑study work visa and review immigration detention. TEXT_F: Border and migration restrictions (1,000 extra border staff; full exit checks; tighten short‑term student visas; retain cap on non‑EU workers; English requirement for public‑facing roles; two‑year wait for in‑work benefits for new EU arrivals). Security and order emphasis (stronger terror controls; mandatory deradicalisation for Syria returnees; tougher hate‑crime laws; protect neighbourhood policing). Defence traditionalism (maintain a minimum, credible independent nuclear deterrent). Sovereignty‑minded EU stance (reforms, red‑card for national parliaments; no power transfers without an in/out referendum). Also protects the Human Rights Act/ECHR and advances LGBT rights.",
